                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is Geometry Wars mixed with Rogue Legacy. \n\nEverytime you die, you start over from the first level but keep your upgrades and can buy new upgrades with the money you made from a run.\n\nFeatures:\n[*]You can customize your ship with new hull components, weapons, secondary weapons...\n[*]Ship changes appearance based on the weapons you carry.\n[*]You can level up and buy upgrades in a skill tree\n[*]You can reroll the attributes of an item.\n[*]You can switch between 4 main weapons (gatlin gun, laser, particle cannon, phaser arrays...)\n[*]You have a secondary weapon like missiles, mines, drones....\n[*]You have a super that allows you to throw bombs, grenades, clustergrenades...\n[*]Randomized level generation which is reminiscent of FTL (you travel between nodes)\n[*]Level modifiers like area size, enemy size, exp gained, player damage, enemy damage but also environmental effects like black holes or meteor storms.\n\nIt's quite the ambitious project! And it mostly delivers! One of the downsides is (and why a lot of people would give it a pass) is that the graphics don't look great. If you can look past that, I think you'd be pleasantly surprised.",
